<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lakilaponto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Sultan Murhum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lakilaponto was the sixth king of Buton, an island state off south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a>, and its first sultan. Around 1540 he adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> under the influence of a teacher from the Malay world and took the name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Murhum, turning the kingdom into the Sultanate of Buton. Tradition credits him with defending Buton against outside raiders and laying the foundations of its later institutions.</p></div>
